Tidy← {
 ⍝H Tidy (fn)
 ⍝H {res}← [opts] ∇ source 
 ⍝H ∘  Aligns comments nicely in dfn or tradfn source (and code generally),
 ⍝H    distinguishing between left-hand side (LHS) comments and right-hand 
 ⍝H    side (RHS), so that RHS comments can be aligned all together.
 ⍝H ∘  Unlike other similar software, it can locate the comments in any 
 ⍝H    desired comment and can even calculate a "best" position, for cases
 ⍝H    where few source lines are wide enough to cause difficulty.
 ⍝H ∘  Handles arbitrary char. vectors of vectors, files, and in-workspace 
 ⍝H    fns and ops.
 ⍝  For more information, see bottom of this function. 
  1 22 911:: ⎕SIGNAL⊂⎕DMX.('EN'EN ⋄ 'Message'Message)
    ⍝ Initialise
      ⎕IO ⎕ML← 0 1
      ⍺← ()
    'help'≡⍺: ⎕ED '_'⊣ _← '^\h*⍝H\h?(.*)' ⎕S ' \1'⊢ ⎕NR ⊃⎕XSI 
    ⍝ Variables, defined  
      fnOpÊ←  ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown function or operator' )
      optÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Unknown option(s)' )
      tabÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Invalid tab value' )
      fixÊ←   ⊂( 'EN'  11 ⋄ 'Message' 'Can''t fix object' )
      LogicÊ← ⊂( 'EN' 911 ⋄ 'Message' 'Logic error' )
      o← (                                       ⍝ Default options
        tab: 'b' ⋄ inc: 5 ⋄ min: 20 ⋄ dcm: 1 ⋄ fi: 0 
        pctile: 95 ⋄ compact: 50 ⋄ gap: ¯1 ⋄ inPlace: 1      
      )
    ⍝ Functions, defined. (namespace o is an implicit arg of all fns) 
      ∆Tidy← ∇                                   ⍝ This function ("me")
      FOF← {                                     ⍝ FOF: in-core fn/op or file?
        ~o.fi: _← {                              ⍝ File with code of any type
            ~⍵ ⎕NC⍛∊ 3 4: ⎕SIGNAL fnOpÊ
              ll← o ∆Tidy 62 ⎕ATX ⍵              ⍝ Get ⍵ and process.  
            ~o.inPlace: _← ll  
            0≠ ⊃0⍴⎕FX ll: _← ll                  ⍝ Fix the updated lines & validate...
              ⎕SIGNAL fixÊ 
        }⍵
            o.fi← 0                              ⍝ In-core function
            ll← o ∆Tidy ⊃⎕NGET ⍵ 1               ⍝ Get and process
            _← ll⊂⍛⎕NPUT⍣o.inPlace⊢ ⍵ 1          ⍝ Rewrite in place (if o.inPlace=1) 
        1: _← ll     
      }
      AL← {                                      ⍝ AL: Align line
          ∆ p← ⍺ ⍵                               ⍝ ∆: Pad by at least ∆ spaces. 
        p≤o.tab: ''⍴⍨ ∆⌈ ¯1+ o.tab- p        
          ''⍴⍨ ∆⌈ ¯1+ o.inc| p- o.tab       
      }
      AT← (⌊0.5∘+){                              ⍝ AT: Generate Absolute Tab  
        0=⊃0⍴⍺: ⍺ ⋄ f← ⊃⍺               
          in out← ↓⍉↑(       
            '''[^'']*''' '&'
            '\h*⍝.*$'    ''
            '\h*$'       ''
          )
          LL← {                                  ⍝ LL: Longest lines, length of w/ pctiles
              ⍺← 100                             ⍝ ⍺/p: What %age of ll. 
              isB← ⍵⍵='b'                        ⍝ isB: isBest option?        
              p xtra← ⍺ ⍺⍺                       ⍝ ⍺⍺/xtra: # spaces to add (or remove, if xtra<0)
              max← ⌈/ll← ≢¨in ⎕R out⊢ ⍵          ⍝ line lengths 
              compact← max≤ o.compact 
            ⍝ o.gap default is 5 if compact. 1 otherwise.
              gap← xtra+ (o.gap< 0)⊃ o.gap (compact⊃ 1 5)
              P← { i←100÷⍨p×¯1+≢⍵ ⋄ R 0.5× ⍵[⌊i]+ ⍵[⌈i] } ⍝ Pctile (rounded)
              R← ⌊0.5∘+                          ⍝ Round
              S← ⊂∘⍋⍛⌷                           ⍝ Sort 
            p= 100: gap+ max 
            isB∧ compact: gap+ 1+ max            ⍝ Line is so compact, "best" is on the right.
            p≥ 100: gap+ R 0.01× p× max          ⍝ % (not %ile) if above 100% 
              gap+ P S ll                        ⍝ Actual interpolated percentile
          } 
          V←  ⊃∘⌽∘⎕VFI                           ⍝ Value
      ⍝ "Best" line length is  o.pctile-th %ile of input line lengths.
        f∊ 'bB': o.pctile (1 LL 'b') ⍵           ⍝ tab set to "best" line length plus 1.
        f∊ '+-×': ((0 LL f) ⍵) (⍎f) V 1↓⍺        ⍝ tab is relative to exact max line length.
          V ⍺                                    ⍝ Absolute positioning
      }
      TB← { +/∧\' '= ⌽⍵ }                        ⍝ TB: Trailing blanks
      LB← { +/∧\' '=  ⍵ }                        ⍝ LB: Leading blanks 
      RF← {                                      ⍝ RF: Regex Field value
        ⍺.Lengths[⍵]↑ ⍺.Offsets[⍵]↓ ⍺.Block 
      } 
⍝ Main, Preamble                              
  ×≢⊃~/(⍺ o).⎕NL ¯2: ⎕SIGNAL optÊ                ⍝ Does user bring only valid options?
      _← o ⎕NS ⍺                                 ⍝ Merge in user options
  1≥≡ ⍵: FOF ,⍵                                  ⍝ FOF handles fns (fi:0), files (fi:1).
      o.tab← o.tab AT ⍵                          ⍝ Calculate the absolute tab pos'n.
      cur← 0                                     ⍝ cur:     Our cur pos'n on this line.
      noCod← 1                                   ⍝ noCod:   Just code on the line of ⍵?
      stI cdI lcI dcmI cmI spI ← ⍳≢pats← (       ⍝ Our patterns...
        '^'                                      ⍝    stI: start    (of line)
        '''[^'']*''|[^⍝''\h]+'                   ⍝    cdI:  code     (fragments)
        '\h*⍝⍝.*$'                               ⍝    lcI: literal comment (don't format)
        o.dcm⊃ (                                 ⍝    dcmI: double comments
          '(*F)'                                 ⍝    ← nop pattern, i.e. ignore                      
          '(\h*⍝.+?\h{5,})((?<!⍝)⍝(?!⍝).*)$'     ⍝    ← active pattern. ≥5 spaces between   
        )      
        '\h*⍝.*$'                                ⍝ cmI: comment  (w/ preceding spaces)
        '\h+(?!⍝)'                               ⍝ spI: spaces (not before comments)
      )
      DblCm← {                                   ⍝ "Double" comments (see details)
        cm1 cm2← ⍵ RF¨ 1 2                       ⍝ ... get LHS and RHS comments
        cm1↓⍨← -TB cm1                           ⍝ ... Remove trail. blanks from LHS...
        pad← 5 AL cur+ ≢cm1                      ⍝ ... align "2nd" comment on RHS
        cm1, pad, cm2   
      }
    ⍝ Pattern matching scan 
      Executive← pats ⎕R {  
          m← ⍵.Match
          Case← ⍵.PatternNum∘=
        Case stI: m ⊣ cur⊢← 0  ⊣ noCod⊢← 1       ⍝ Start of line
        Case cdI: m ⊣ cur+← ≢m ⊣ noCod⊢← 0       ⍝ Code found
        Case lcI: m ⊣ cur+← ≢m                   ⍝ literal comment '⍝⍝'
        Case spI: m ⊣ cur+← ≢m                   ⍝ Spaces (not foll by comment)
      ⍝ Last two cases consume rest of line; cur is reset at stI above.
        Case dcmI: DblCm ⍵                       ⍝ Double comment 
       ~Case cmI: ⎕SIGNAL LogicÊ                 ⍝ cmI: Default comments below ↓↓↓
          nsp← LB m                                        
        noCod∧ o.min> cur+ nsp: m                ⍝ If LHS comment, return as is
          m↓⍨← nsp                               ⍝ If RHS comment 
          m,⍨  1 AL cur                          ⍝ ... align at a valid tab stop.
      }  
    ⍝ Main Executive
      Executive ⍵

  ⍝  Rest of "help" information
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H Syntax: 
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯      
  ⍝H {res}← [opts] ∇ source                 
  ⍝H   source: [sourceDoc | sourceFnOp | sourceFi]
  ⍝H   opts:   ( tab: 'best' ⋄ inc: 5  ⋄ min: 20  ⋄ dcm: 1 ⋄ fi: 0 ⋄ pctile: 95 )
  ⍝H   res:    the modified source document as a shy char vector of vectors result. 
  ⍝H           As a "side" effect, updates fns, opts, and files IN PLACE. 
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H Other features:
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H ∘ Allows "double" comments, i.e. those with both
  ⍝H   a LHS comment (starting with ⍝) and a RHS comment (ditto). (See dcm: 1)
  ⍝H ∘ Can place comments in the "best" position, where some code lines
  ⍝H   are far longer than the average. (See tab: 'best')
  ⍝H ∘ LHS comments are never moved.
  ⍝H ∘ RHS comments that start with ⍝⍝H (double ⍝) are never moved,
  ⍝H   even within "double" comments.
  ⍝H ∘ If the longest lines are shorter than ¨compact¨ number of bytes,
  ⍝H   (compact: 50) by default, the "best" position will be just to the 
  ⍝H   right of ALL lines.   (See compact option).
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H right argument (⍵):
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H source:   'line1' 'line2' ... | 'Fn/Op Name' | 'File.typ' when (fi: 1)
  ⍝H   sourceDoc:   CVV  The source text to format. The updated doc is returned.
  ⍝H   sourceFnOp:  CV   The name of a function or operator with the code to format; requires (fi:0).   
  ⍝H                     The updated fn/op text is fixed and returned shyly.
  ⍝H   sourceFi:    CV   The name of a file with the code to format; requires (fi:1).  
  ⍝H                     It is updated IN PLACE.
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H options (⍺):
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H   tab:   column in which to put comments if possible; 
  ⍝H          defaults to 'best', typically the 95th percentile on line lengths.
  ⍝H   tab:   dd | '-dd' '+dd' '×d.dd' 'best' (or 'b'), where d is a digit.
  ⍝H        Format   Tab value      Notes 
  ⍝H       'dd'|dd   tab← dd        dd, an integer, here indicating exact tab column.
  ⍝H         '+dd'   tab← ll+dd     ll, the length of the longest input line
  ⍝H         '-dd'   tab← ll-dd     ll, the length of the longest input line
  ⍝H        '×d.dd'  tab← ll×d.dd   d.dd, a small float/int string used to scale ll.
  ⍝H        'best'   tab← pctile    dd is 1 past the dd-th percentile of input line lengths.
  ⍝H                                By default: (pctile: 95), the 95th percentile.
  ⍝H   inc:   If code text extends to <tab> or beyond, place comments multiples
  ⍝H           of <inc> to the right of position <tab>.
  ⍝H   min:   Treat any comments before column <min> as fixed LHS comments. Defaults to 20.
  ⍝H   fi:    If 1 and ⍵ has depth ≤1, treats ⍵ as the name of a file to update in place (see below).
  ⍝H          Otherwise, a char vector right arg is treated as a fn or operator name.
  ⍝H          If ⍵ is a CVV (has multiple lines), fi is ignored.
  ⍝H   dcm:   If 1, will recognize pairs of comments on a line, 
  ⍝H            - the "first" will be treated as a LHS comment, and
  ⍝H            - the "second" will be aligned with the other RHS comments. 
  ⍝H            - The two must be have at least five blanks in between. 
  ⍝H          If 0, any comment is treated as either LHS or RHS comment.
  ⍝H  pctile: Unless (tab: 'best') is set, pctile is ignored.
  ⍝H          If (tab: 'best'), the default percentile length is used, 
  ⍝H          viz. (pctile: 95) plus 1.
  ⍝H          ∘ The pctile refers to the interpolated %ile of the length of all
  ⍝H            the lines in the input. 
  ⍝H            (Above 100%, a percentage above the longest line is used).)
  ⍝H          ∘ You can change pctile to any positive integer, where 
  ⍝H            100 is the 100th pctile, 90 is the 90%ile, and 120 is 120% of the max. 
  ⍝H Example of pairs: 
  ⍝H This is a fixed LHS comment              ⍝⍝H this RHS comment won't move     
  ⍝H This is a LHS comment                       ⍝H This RHS comment will move if (dcm: 1)
  ⍝H ---------------------------------
  ⍝H Notes:
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H 1. If source is a char vector of vectors, it is treated as 
  ⍝H    multiline APL code (a fn, op, or set of code objects)
  ⍝H    a.  Returns the source with comments aligned per options.
  ⍝H 2. If source is a char. vector, and...
  ⍝H    a.  if (fi: 0), the default:
  ⍝H        - ⍵ refers to the name of a visible function;
  ⍝H        - its source representation (verbatim if possible) is formatted and...
  ⍝H          - returned as a shy value;
  ⍝H          - the function is also refixed for you. 
  ⍝H    b.  if (fi: 1):
  ⍝H        - ⍵ refers to a file, which is read;
  ⍝H        - its source is formatted and...
  ⍝H          - rewritten to the file (in place) and
  ⍝H          - returned as a shy value.
  ⍝H ------------------------------------
  ⍝H Documentation: 
  ⍝H ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯
  ⍝H   To see this information, call: Tidy⍨'help'  
  ⍝H
}
